body:
Okay, I've reviewed the original code that causes the issue. It's [these lines](https://github.com/thenativeweb/reqd/blob/60d8a45ed7e6ba9af3a222d7bd813dd209a328ce/app.js#L25-L29) that cause the issue:

```
if (!stats.isDirectory()) {
  /*eslint-disable consistent-return*/
  return;
  /*eslint-enable consistent-return*/
}
```

If I remove the ESLint comments, everything is fine (okay, then I get another error about an inconsistent `return`, but that's another story).

PS: Sorry for not having posted the exact code right from the start :-/

issue.body:
With `padded-blocks` set to `"never"` the following is reported as a warning and should not be:

``` js
if (a){
  // i'm a comment!
 let b = c
}
```

Removing the comment allows the rule to pass. The problem does not exist with the default eslint parser.
